# Guidance — webMethods Documentation Agent (09)

RGV loop (DRY source), artifact extraction patterns, and few-shot examples for webMethods AS-IS specification generation.

---

## SECTION 1: RGV LOOP (DRY — Single Source of Truth)

Every section in Phases 1-5 MUST follow this exact loop. Referenced from `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc`.

```
FOR EACH section to generate:
  1. RE-READ  — Fresh Read tool call on ALL relevant artifact files for this section
  2. INVENTORY — Count target elements in artifact, list names, COMMIT to count N
                 State: "This {artifact} has N {elements}. I will generate exactly N items."
  3. GENERATE — Produce section content (must contain exactly N items)
  4. VERIFY  — Count generated items, compare to N
  5. FIX     — If mismatch → RE-READ artifact, find missing, fix BEFORE proceeding
  6. CHECKPOINT — Emit micro-checkpoint: ✅ {section}: {Name} — N/N {elements}
```

**Rules:**
- If VERIFY shows X ≠ N → do NOT proceed. RE-READ and FIX first.
- Each section is an **ATOMIC UNIT** — complete one before starting the next.
- Never generate from memory or stale Phase 0 context — always RE-READ fresh.
- For related artifacts (e.g., FLOW + its NDF signatures), read ALL related files together before generating.

