## SECTION 6: FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES

### Flow Step Documentation

❌ **BAD — Vague:**
```markdown
Step 3: Invokes a service to look up data
```

✅ **GOOD — Complete:**
```markdown
| Step | Type | Name | Description | Properties | Previous | Next | Pipeline Impact |
|------|------|------|-------------|------------|----------|------|----------------|
| 3 | INVOKE | pub.partner:lookupPartner | Invokes partner lookup service using partnerId from pipeline | `service="pub.partner:lookupPartner"` | MAP step 2 | BRANCH step 4 (success) | Reads: `/request/partnerId`; Creates: `/partnerDetails/*` |
```

**Why:** Includes type, fully qualified service name, properties, connectivity, and pipeline effects.

### NDF Classification

❌ **BAD — Assumed from path:**
```markdown
node.ndf in services folder → must be a Flow Service
```

✅ **GOOD — Classified from content:**
```markdown
**Type:** DocType (NDF)
**Evidence:** `rec_fields` element present with 8 field definitions; no `svc_type` attribute found.
**Fields:** 8 (3 required, 5 optional)
```

**Why:** Classification is evidence-based, not assumed from folder structure.

### Mapping Tables

❌ **BAD — Summarized:**
```markdown
Key mappings (showing 3 of 15):
| Source | Target |
| /request/id | /response/id |
| (12 more follow same pattern...) |
```

✅ **GOOD — Complete:**
```markdown
#### Field Mappings — pub.transform:mapOrderRequest

| # | Source Field | Source Path | Target Field | Target Path | Type | Notes |
|---|-------------|-------------|--------------|-------------|------|-------|
| 1 | id | /request/id | orderId | /order/orderId | Direct | |
| 2 | customerName | /request/customer/name | custName | /order/custName | Direct | |
...
| 15 | statusCode | /request/status | orderStatus | /order/orderStatus | Conditional | Needs verification |
```

**Why:** ALL 15 mappings documented individually. Never abbreviate or summarize.

### ACL Analysis

❌ **BAD — Generic:**
```markdown
ACL file defines permissions for services.
```

✅ **GOOD — Specific:**
```markdown
| Node | executeACL | readACL | writeACL | listACL | Runtime Impact |
|------|-----------|---------|----------|---------|---------------|
| pub.services:processOrder | Internal | Internal | Internal | Internal | Internal-only — not externally callable |
| pub.services.pub:submitOrder | Anonymous | Anonymous | Internal | Anonymous | Externally callable — exposed endpoint |
```

**Why:** Per-node mapping with derived runtime impact.

### Cross-Artifact Synthesis — Call Chain

❌ **BAD — Flat list:**
```markdown
Services used: serviceA, serviceB, serviceC
```

✅ **GOOD — Ordered graph:**
```markdown
#### End-to-End Call Chain

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[pub:receiveOrder<br/>Entry - SOAP endpoint] --> B[pub.transform:mapRequest<br/>MAP - Input transformation]
    B --> C[pub.partner:lookupPartner<br/>INVOKE - Partner DB lookup]
    C --> D{pub.routing:routeOrder<br/>BRANCH - Route by region}
    D -->|EU| E[pub.eu:processEU<br/>INVOKE - EU processing]
    D -->|US| F[pub.us:processUS<br/>INVOKE - US processing]
    E --> G[pub.response:buildResponse<br/>MAP - Response transformation]
    F --> G
```

**Why:** Shows execution order, branching, and service roles with fully qualified names.

### Extensionless WSDL Detection

❌ **BAD — Skipped:**
```markdown
File `wsdl0` has no recognized extension — skipping.
```

✅ **GOOD — Content-inspected:**
```markdown
**File:** `ws/visualiserPartenaire/wsdl0`
**Detection:** Extensionless file. Content inspection: `<wsdl:definitions>` root element found.
**Classified as:** WSDL
**Target namespace:** `http://example.com/visualiserPartenaire`
**Operations:** 3 (getPartenaire, updatePartenaire, deletePartenaire)
```

**Why:** Content-based classification catches extensionless artifacts that would otherwise be missed.

### REST Resource Handler Documentation

❌ **BAD — Generic:**
```markdown
REST service handler found in restServices/_post.
```

✅ **GOOD — Structured extraction:**
```markdown
### Flow: restServices._post (REST Resource Handler)

**Source:** `ns/.../restServices/_post/flow.xml`
**Pattern:** REST resource definition — uses `_post` folder convention for HTTP POST method handler.

**Input MAP — 7 MAPSET operations:**

| # | Target Field | Set Value | Purpose |
|---|-------------|-----------|---------|
| 1 | /documentTypeNameRequete | pkg.schema:requestDocType | Request schema docType reference |
| 2 | /documentTypeNameReponse | pkg.schema:responseDocType | Response schema docType reference |
| 3 | /serviceOperation | pkg.services.pub:mainService | Target operation service |
...

> ⚠️ GAP: `frmkcommon.restUtil:postXmlService` — external framework dependency, not in scanned project.
```

**Why:** Documents framework delegation, all MAPSET configurations, and flags external dependencies.

### Schema-Derived DocType Documentation

❌ **BAD — Fields only:**
```markdown
DocType BornesElecType has 2 fields: BorneInferieure, BorneSuperieure.
```

✅ **GOOD — With schema metadata:**
```markdown
**Type:** DocType (NDF) — Schema-derived
**Evidence:** `rec_fields` present, `schemaType`, `schemaDomain`, no `svc_type`

| # | Field Name | Type | Nillable | Namespace | Content Type Reference |
|---|-----------|------|----------|-----------|----------------------|
| 1 | tns:BorneInferieure | string | false | http://...v2 | typeStringMin1Max13 |
| 2 | tns:BorneSuperieure | string | false | http://...v2 | typeStringMin1Max13 |

**Schema Metadata:**
| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| schemaType.xmlns | http://...v2 |
| schemaType.ncName | BornesElecType |
| schemaDomain | visualiserResponse |
| originURI | file:///...xsd |
```

**Why:** Schema metadata is essential for understanding XSD-to-DocType lineage.

### Custom ACL Documentation

❌ **BAD — Standard assumption:**
```markdown
| Node | executeACL | Runtime Impact |
| ws:service | PscWS | Externally callable |
```

✅ **GOOD — Custom ACL noted:**
```markdown
| Node | executeACL | readACL | Runtime Impact |
| ws:service | **PscWS** | **PscWS** | **Custom ACL** — externally callable with PscWS role (project-specific, not Anonymous) |
| restServices:_post | **PscWS** | **PscWS** | **Custom ACL** — REST endpoint requires PscWS role |
```

**Why:** Custom ACL names have different security implications than Anonymous. Always bold and note "Custom ACL".

