## SECTION 7: ARCHITECTURE COMPLIANCE CHECKLIST

### Pre-Certification Validation (Run before Phase 6)

- [ ] All artifact files in project folder were scanned and classified
- [ ] Extensionless files were content-inspected (not skipped)
- [ ] All NDF files were subtype-classified from content (not assumed from path)
- [ ] All flow steps documented with full properties and connectivity
- [ ] All NDF signatures include ALL fields (not just "key" fields)
- [ ] All mapping tables are complete (no summarization)
- [ ] All ACL entries include runtime impact derivation
- [ ] Cross-artifact synthesis includes call chain, contracts, mappings, dependencies
- [ ] Every extraction cites source file and element
- [ ] Missing artifacts explicitly stated as "Not present in provided artifacts"
- [ ] Unresolvable references flagged as GAP entries
- [ ] Duplicate structures (schemasWithoutPrefixes, .bak files) noted but not double-counted
- [ ] Custom ACL names identified and runtime impact documented
- [ ] Multi-package projects: all sub-packages processed, cross-package dependencies tracked
- [ ] REST resource handlers: framework delegation documented, external services flagged as GAP
- [ ] Schema-derived DocTypes: schema metadata (schemaType, schemaDomain, originURI) extracted
- [ ] Micro-checkpoint counts match across all phases
- [ ] webMethods documentation hyperlinks included for major concepts
- [ ] `java.frag` files detected and noted as base64-encoded (not skipped or treated as `.java`)
- [ ] MAP sub-operations (mapcopy/mapset/mapdelete/mapmove/mapinsert) documented per MAP step with source/target
- [ ] MAP modes (input/output/standalone/invokeinput/invokeoutput) identified and documented for INVOKE steps
- [ ] Transformer patterns (service call inside MAP step) identified and documented as embedded service calls
- [ ] Trigger nodes in `ns/.../triggers/` folders scanned, classified, and extraction performed (§3.11)
- [ ] `irtnode_property` base64-decoded for adapter services where `svc_subtype` is unclear or adapter details are sparse

